# Mob architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/mobs.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/mobs.md).

**Permanent decision:** **mobs ≠ NPCs.** Mobs are PVE combatants (monsters,
animals, fauna). In shared space they are **cell entities** — network-synced
via interest so peers **see and help** the same fight / boss HP. Cell owns
aggro, HP, death, loot, leash, kill/assist credit. **Editor** places dens
(Build Web); **Server Console** owns MobDef / loot / packs. LOD + AI budgets
on web. Not player Sidekick. Ship Combat = different loop.
[NPCs](../../docs/docs/architecture/npc.md),
[Missions](../../docs/docs/architecture/missions.md) (kill / escort credit),
[Loot tables](../../docs/docs/architecture/loot-tables.md),
[Progression](../../docs/docs/architecture/progression.md) (kill XP),
[Factions](../../docs/docs/architecture/factions.md),
[Multiplayer](../../docs/docs/architecture/multiplayer.md),
[Content delivery](../../docs/docs/architecture/content-delivery.md).

When changing mob spawn, AI, PVE combat, loot, dens, or wildlife catalog,
read the full doc first. Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
